# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which endpoint the demo talks to.
#
#   relaxai    Civo relaxAI (the default, and the point of the SDK)
#   ollama     a local open-weight model on Ollama — no account, no key
#   lmstudio   LM Studio's local server
#   llamacpp   llama.cpp's llama-server
#
# Case-insensitive. An unrecognised value stops the app with a message listing
# the valid ones; it does NOT fall back to relaxAI.
#
# Put this file at examples/next-app/.env.local — Next reads env files from the
# app directory, not the repository root — and restart the dev server after
# changing it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELAX_UI_PROVIDER=relaxai

# Optional, for any provider. Unset: relaxAI uses Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E, and
# a local provider asks the runtime what is installed and picks the smallest
# model that can still manage a nested document.
# RELAX_UI_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# --- relaxAI ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://relax.ai. Read on the server only — never prefix a key
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_, which would ship it to every browser that loads the page.
RELAX_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to https://api.relax.ai/v1. The sovereignty guard refuses
# any host not on its allowlist, so this cannot silently point elsewhere.
# RELAX_BASE_URL=https://api.relax.ai/v1

# --- local runtimes (NOT sovereign endpoints) --------------------------------
# No API key is needed. The sovereignty guard still runs: a local provider
# carries a loopback-only allowlist, so these may point at a different *port*
# on this machine but not at another host. Reaching a remote runtime needs an
# explicit `sovereignty.allowedHosts` in code — an environment variable cannot
# widen the allowlist. The UI says plainly that you are not on a sovereign
# endpoint.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1
# LLAMACPP_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
